<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Eliot (missionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1604–1690</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Eliot (1604–1690) was an English Puritan minister in the Massachusetts Bay Colony, known as the &quot;Apostle to the Indians&quot;. He learned the Massachusett language, preached to Native communities from 1646 and organised settlements of Christian Native people known as praying towns, beginning with Natick in 1651. His translation of the Bible into Massachusett, printed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a> in 1663, was the first complete Bible printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-eliot-missionary.jpg" alt="John Eliot (missionary)" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_John_Eliot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
